'''First Sartan Civil War''' refers to the civil war in Sarta that lasted from 1738 to 1747.

The conflict emerged from baronial rivalry, popular unrest, and disputes over the authority of [[Maria I of Sarta]]'s regime. It followed the post-[[Treaty of Bahia Alta]] political settlement and intensified divisions between inland royalists, parliamentary supporters, and elites with ties to [[Volisania]].

The war devastated the countryside and strained the urban economy. It ended in 1747 with Maria I of Sarta consolidating control through the royal parliamentary court.

